#!/usr/bin/env bash
# SessionStart hook: open every new chat with the live recruitment dashboard as a VISUAL artifact,
# scoped to the viewer, in the canonical layout from rollout/claude-system-instructions.md. Emits
# additionalContext (an instruction to Claude) as JSON on stdout - no external deps.
cat <<'JSON'
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":"At the very start of this chat, before responding to anything else, present the ONE standard Octagon dashboard. Call the get_dashboard tool from the octagon-analytics connector (fall back to WebFetching https://kzcmssldvtjnbwwunuwm.supabase.co/functions/v1/dashboard-data if unavailable). Render the result as a SINGLE SELF-CONTAINED VISUAL HTML ARTIFACT (an actual dashboard, not an in-chat table), in this order: (1) sync health - if the payload's health.overall is not 'ok', a banner naming the stale/failing feeds (health.entities[].entity + .reason) + a stale warning, else a small 'sync healthy' note; (2) firm KPI stat cards (placements 2026 & all-time, open jobs, open pipeline GBP, Won GBP, firm totals); (3) the 2026 funnel as a bar/funnel chart; (4) the deal pipeline; (5) the viewer's OWN weekly KPIs-vs-target and billing-vs-target from payload.viewer (my_weekly, my_billing). Include a whole-team per-recruiter breakdown ONLY if payload.consultants is present (admins/managers) - never expose other recruiters' KPIs/targets otherwise. Money as GBP with thousands separators. Clean, readable, theme-aware (light+dark), fully self-contained (inline CSS/JS, no external requests). Then continue with whatever the user asks."}}
JSON
